 "images": {
  "1107": "sha256:3f32a962ce04b7c8d85337cd427a8946b8b6bcaadd97cc8d8a8cd14e8d68a6ce",
  "candidate-47": "the same image with the 26 candidate-47 files (0762..0769 applied to its tree) bind-mounted read-only; ../common/overlay-sha.txt"
 },
 "evidence": "One session on sp4, ABBA (1107 boot1, c47 boot1, c47 boot2, 1107 boot2): the PR's bench_moe_l2_evict.py verbatim (bench-*.txt), then our harness h966.py (h966-*.json), which builds the PR bench's plans and FFN layer with the PR's own build_plan and times the image-default plan (and, on the candidate image, explicit evict_normal and evict_first plans, interleaved window by window) eagerly, by CUDA-graph replay of the layer (the bench's eager L2 prefetch before each replay) and by one graph of 16 back-to-back layers without prefetch, 15 windows x 16 layers. Output hashes compared across images.",
 "readme_command_defects": [
  "The README's benchmark command runs the plain spark-ds41f:1107 image with only the bench mounted; on 1107 the bench fails before any timing (TypeError: grouped_fp8_fp4_gemm() got an unexpected keyword argument 'eviction_policy'), both boots. It needs the patched moe.py, i.e. the candidate image",
  "The README says each point is 5 interleaved (baseline, candidate) pairs of 32 timed iterations after 10 warmups; the script times each arm once (16 warmups, 64 timed calls), baseline first, not interleaved",
  "The README's FFN tables include M=64; the script's FFN loop stops at M=32",
  "On the candidate image both of the bench's arms carry 0765's moe_swiglu_cast, so its A/B is candidate-47 with and without 0763"
 ],
